{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1471510-complete-a-gift-roll","id":1471510,"title":"Complete a gift roll","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-30T16:58:34-08:00","id":1471510,"title":"Complete a gift roll","content":"Some gifts need a roll to work and measure the effects or duration. When I read the list of the gifts of the shadow lords I saw that a gift of the hakkens allowed to &quot;complete&quot; the result of the roll by spending Rage to improve the effects<br /> <br /> Could we imagine a rule or a gift that would allow to complete the rolls of the other gifts by spending rage, willpower or gnosis? <br /> In the case of vampires by spending extra blood points or willpower via a new discipline power like thaumaturgy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T17:53:11-08:00","id":1471513,"title":"","content":"Obviously it is possible to do - talens and fetishes work this way by default - but I'm not sure it's practical. There are just too many Gifts, with too many iterations of what a roll result means. You would need a much more standardized Gift system to really make this work. As it stands, there's just too many variables to account for. How do you balance a Gift where one success is all you need, but the difficulty is variable, against a Gift where the difficulty is set but the number of successes is vital? And that's just one consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T01:33:01-08:00","id":1471524,"title":"","content":"My first idea was to select only the gift that need many success to work, like fangs of the north, troll skin, mother touch etc... <br /> You roll the gift and can complete it only if its not a botch and maybe only with the same caracteristic as the activation cost, if mother touch need gnosis to activate, you can only complete it with gnosis<br /> The gifts that did not need an activation cost, if just one success is needed to work, in those cases you cannot spend points to complete the roll<br /> <br /> There's many gifts and discipline that depend of other thing so depending of the power itself that ability would be possible or not, the ST has the last word<br /> <br /> Inside the game it would not be crazy to imagine that werewolves and vampires can reinforce the effect of their powers by putting more resources into them, at the risk of losing their strength too quickly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T02:16:12-08:00","id":1471525,"title":"","content":"I get what the idea is. I'm saying that with the sheer volume of Gifts in the game, the effort of implementing the idea is probably not worth it. Especially for the Garou, regaining the resources isn't speedy, and they can burn through some of them extremely quickly. There's no cap on how much Gnosis a Garou can spend in a turn, they can spend half of their Rage rounded up per turn, and only Willpower is capped at 1 per turn (but you can spend WP on the same turn as Gnosis or Rage In three turns a Garou can burn through points that can take them weeks to get back to full (and Losing the Wolf is a problem). They don't have the option of just chowing down on a human like a vampire to top themselves up quickly.<br /> <br /> Garou risk losing their strength too quickly under the current rules already. Making that worse doesn't seem like a good idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T05:35:48-08:00","id":1471530,"title":"","content":"That depense would not be the new only way, only a bonus if the player want to be sure to get what he need, and as you said with the possibility of loosing the wolf it may prevent the players from abusing it. Plus i'm going with the idea of a high ranked gift to do that, not a simple rule.<br /> As the st you can cap how much gnosis can be spent with that gift (1 to 3 could be good)<br /> <br /> However as a talen or fetishe wich give a certain amount of success (depending on the power of the spirit 1 at 5) it could be usefull without being to expensive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T11:02:28-08:00","id":1471546,"title":"","content":"OK... let me try a different question:<br /> <br /> What's the point of this? Is there a problem you're trying to address? Is there a need that you think should be filled? Is this just something cool you want to be able to do more?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T16:42:41-08:00","id":1471692,"title":"","content":"Not really, i'm only trying to create new powers that my players can discover by exploring the umbra. We're planning to continue the game until the famous final fight again the Wyrm and his forces and some ancients, forgottens, or new powers could be usefull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T19:56:17-08:00","id":1471705,"title":"","content":"So, just to point this out, over four edition something like 750 unique Gifts have been printed for WtA (including ones that are supposed to be rare or lost in modern times in books like Dark Ages, Croatoan Song, and the White Howler Tribebook). Five players could easily have 100 Gifts each without any overlapping Gifts. A lot of that glut of them are meh (or at least in a serious need of revamping if you want to make them work in W20), but it's still a lot of material even for a game with a long time frame intended.<br /> <br /> And really, if you want to get into strange Gifts to find in the Umbra, I'd say start with Rage Across the Heavens. You don't have to use those Gifts in particular, but they are prime examples of the kind of Gift you're talking about there. And they're a lot more evocative than &quot;buy a Gift that just makes one of your other Gifts better.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}